title: justifying deleted content rels, and marking them okay
pid: 84508eeb-aa53-4ca6-8e3d-695d553f84ab
body: |2-
  If N contained C, D and E, and now M contains C and D,
  then N's content in the diff view shows the usual ghosts,
  but also it should show 'ghosts' shared containers':
  ```
    * N
    ** <a>'s lost content <1:2..> share the container <1:1 / 1>
    *** the common container
    **** M
    ***** these contain it
    ****** M' which contains M
    ******* M'' which contains M' ...
    **** (ghost) C
    **** (ghost) D
    ** (ghost) C
    ** (ghost) D
    ** (ghost) E
  ```
  Cycling the commit-readiness of the relationship from N to C
  should work from either ghost image of C.
  Cycling the "which share the container" node's commit-readiness
  should mark the relationship from N to C and D.
